  "_comment": "Named OpenAI Codex logins, pinned across lib/pure/codex.js (GNOME), claude-code/codex-contract.js (CLI + MCP) and ClaudeUsageCore/Codex.swift (macOS). A Codex profile is one saved `auth.json` from the Codex home ($CODEX_HOME, else ~/.codex). Identity comes out of the id token's claims, read WITHOUT verifying the signature - the file is one only this user can write, and the claims are used for nothing but naming the account and its plan. tokenState never triggers an exchange: unlike the Claude store, nothing here mints a Codex token, so a stale one is reported and left to `codex login`. `limits` pins the ONLY usage numbers this project will show for Codex: the rate limits the Codex CLI itself recorded when the API last told it, marked estimated and stamped with when they were captured. There is no case in which a number is invented.",
